If we specify the @destroy adverb, we must be in --destroy mode.
This is a one time, transient adverb while you make a change.

Once it has been destroyed, you can remove the **WHOLE** element from the script
so it will not be re-created, OR you can remove **JUST** the @destroy and it will
be created again.  You **CAN** use this to rename something (but there should also be @oldname).

	target destroy_something

		ensure test.S3.Bucket "hello"
			@teardown delete // we need a teardown for this node to qualify "how" to destroy it
			// there is no @destroy on this so cannot use --destroy